<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Distilled water                                        </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;940.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Mix components thoroughly, sparge the medium with a N<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (80:20, v/v) gas mixture and autoclave under the same gas mixture. After cooling, aseptically and anaerobically add the following solutions from sterile anaerobic stocks (autoclaved or *filter-sterilized):  <br>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 8% NaHCO<sub>3</sub> solution*                                  </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;25.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 10% Glucose solution                                     </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;5.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 10% Yeast extract (Oxoid) solution                       </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;5.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 1.0 M Sodium thiosulfate solution                        </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;5.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Trace vitamins* (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=197">197</a>)                  </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;10.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Prior to use, add per liter the following solution (autoclaved and stored under a N<sub>2</sub> atmosphere):  <br>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 5% L-Cysteine&#183;HCl&#183;H<sub>2</sub>O solution            </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;5.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Adjust pH to 6.5, if necessary.  <br>
